143 0 obj
<</E(> The Binary Search Tree \(BST\) was successfully implemented to store and search government identification numbers. The experiment showed that BST search can require fewer comparisons than linear search when the tree structure is suitable. It also demonstrated that the insertion order affects the height of the BST and therefore its search performance. A balanced or reasonably shaped BST provides better search efficiency, while a skewed BST can have O\(n\) search time. Thus, BST is a useful data structure for managing and searching a growing collection of identification records when its height is kept under control.)/K[ 2]/P 93 0 R /Pg 22 0 R /S/P/Type/StructElem>>
endobj
